## Codebase Discoveries
TorchSpec DFlash2 training uses the shared DFlash block objective and adds selector cross-entropy over teacher-forced adjacent transitions. When the gold successor is absent from the draft-logit top-K candidate set, training replaces the weakest candidate with gold. Serving does not insert gold.

The online and offline export paths must call state_dict_for_serving and emit bare candidate-selector codebook parameter names. Strict FULL_SHARD conversion rejects missing or unexpected DFlash2 keys and rejects vocabulary pruning before loading.

FULL_SHARD scalar reduction must use a local one-element CUDA tensor rather than a DTensor-backed scalar. Only data-parallel rank zero writes the online serving artifact, and all ranks exchange writer errors before returning.

The exact three-epoch run contains 375 optimizer updates and saves iteration 376 because checkpoint metadata records the next iteration. Final export validates step 375 and latest_checkpointed_iteration 376.

The serving gate's prompt-only results were also strong: the three selected rows produced acceptance lengths 2.909090909090909, 5.333333333333333, and 8.0. This supports the same conclusion without relying only on mid-response canonical prefixes.

